From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: disp_pwm: invert the backlight level on the Titan Pocket

On the Titan Pocket (project g66v71c2k) the brightness slider works
backwards with this tree: LunaDisplayManager sends rising levels
(disp_pwm_set_backlight_cmdq level_1024 0..1023, in the right direction)
and the panel gets darker.

The stock kernel enables AGOLD_CP2166_LCM_BACKLIGHT for this project,
which the reconstructed tree does not have: the panel module's CP2166
backlight driver reads the display PWM with inverted sense, and stock
compensates. The Titan Slim's equivalent (IS31FL, g83v71c2k) was
recovered from the stock binary in 88eec0cf7f4a; nothing was for g66.

Flip every non-zero level for the g66 projects. 0 is left alone, so the
PWM is still disabled for blanking exactly as before.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/common/pwm10/ddp_pwm.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/common/pwm10/ddp_pwm.c
@@ -631,6 +631,17 @@
 
 		level_1024 = disp_pwm_level_remap(id, level_1024);
 
+#ifdef USE_CP2166_INVERTED_PWM
+		/*
+		 * The CP2166 backlight driver on the Titan Pocket's panel
+		 * module reads the PWM duty inverted: more duty, less light.
+		 * Flip every non-zero level; 0 still disables the PWM below,
+		 * which is what blanking relies on.
+		 */
+		if (level_1024 > 0)
+			level_1024 = 1024 - level_1024;
+#endif
+
 #ifdef USE_IS31FL_LED
 		/* Modified hardware control for g83v71c2k_dfl_eea project */
 		if (level_1024 < 1) {
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/common/pwm10/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/common/pwm10/Makefile
@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@
 obj-y += is31fl.o is31fl_init.o
 endif
 
+# Titan Pocket: the panel module's CP2166 backlight driver reads the display
+# PWM with inverted sense (stock: AGOLD_CP2166_LCM_BACKLIGHT, not in this tree)
+ifneq (,$(filter "g66v71c2k_dfl_eea" "g66v71c2k_dfl_tee",$(CONFIG_ARCH_MTK_PROJECT)))
+ccflags-y += -DUSE_CP2166_INVERTED_PWM=1
+endif
+
 ccflags-y += \
 				-I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/include     \
 				-I$(srctree)/drivers/misc/mediatek/video/common/IPv1     \
